  "name": "Session Waiter Tool Bridge (v1)",
  "description": null,
  "active": true,
  "isArchived": false,
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "bridge-webhook",
      "name": "Bridge Webhook",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.webhook",
      "typeVersion": 2.1,
      "position": [
        240,
        300
      ],
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput",
      "notes": "ADR-066 Block 6: the session-waiter's client-tool servicing entry. The external waiter (Node, services/session-waiter) POSTs a pending client-side custom tool here; this thin wrapper delegates to the SSOT n8n handlers (Triggering Task Tail Handler / ClickUp Extract Tool Handler) and returns the user.custom_tool_result content array. headerAuth (X-Watchdog-Key, the shared waiter<->n8n key) - n8n /webhook/* is public via nginx, so this MUST be authed (the tail handler reads task data with the bot token).",
      "parameters": {
        "httpMethod": "POST",
        "path": "session-waiter-tool-bridge",
        "responseMode": "responseNode",
        "authentication": "headerAuth",
        "options": {}
      },
      "credentials": {
        "httpHeaderAuth": {
          "id": "3ydBksESwiUW2rFV",
          "name": "Storage Watchdog Header Auth"
        }
      },
      "webhookId": "e6fecc67-3eff-4a90-9573-1eb2406f180a"
    },
    {
      "id": "is-extract",
      "name": "Is extract_clickup_task?",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.if",
      "typeVersion": 2.2,
      "position": [
        460,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "Route by tool_name: extract_clickup_task -> ClickUp Extract Tool Handler (caller-scoped REST attachment extraction); everything else (get_task_comments / get_parent_chain / list_attachments / get_attachment / get_task_details) -> Triggering Task Tail Handler. generate_image and clickup_* are in-harness MCP (ADR-055/054) and never reach here.",
      "parameters": {
        "conditions": {
          "options": {
            "caseSensitive": true,
            "leftValue": "",
            "typeValidation": "loose",
            "version": 2
          },
          "combinator": "and",
          "conditions": [
            {
              "id": "c-extract",
              "leftValue": "={{ $json.body.tool_name }}",
              "rightValue": "extract_clickup_task",
              "operator": {
                "type": "string",
                "operation": "equals"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "call-extract-handler",
      "name": "Call Extract Handler",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflow",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        680,
        200
      ],
      "notes": "ADR-054 Block 4b ClickUp Extract Tool Handler (y985MgyA5lCxOFCH). clickup_task_id comes from the agent's tool_input (the related task it wants to read), NOT the triggering task. onError=continueErrorOutput so a failure still resolves the tool (no session deadlock).",
      "parameters": {
        "workflowId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "y985MgyA5lCxOFCH",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "ClickUp Extract Tool Handler (v1)"
        },
        "workflowInputs": {
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "value": {
            "clickup_task_id": "={{ (JSON.parse($json.body.tool_input_json || '{}').clickup_task_id) || '' }}",
            "caller_user_id": "={{ $json.body.caller_user_id }}",
            "clickup_scope": "={{ $json.body.clickup_scope }}"
          },
          "matchingColumns": [],
          "attemptToConvertTypes": false,
          "convertFieldsToString": false
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "id": "call-tail-handler",
      "name": "Call Tail Handler",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.executeWorkflow",
      "typeVersion": 1.3,
      "position": [
        680,
        420
      ],
      "notes": "Triggering Task Tail Handler (Ouo0BlYOw92DUXIh): get_task_comments / get_parent_chain / list_attachments / get_attachment / get_task_details on the triggering task. onError=continueErrorOutput so a failure still resolves the tool (no session deadlock).",
      "parameters": {
        "workflowId": {
          "__rl": true,
          "value": "Ouo0BlYOw92DUXIh",
          "mode": "list",
          "cachedResultName": "Triggering Task Tail Handler (v1)"
        },
        "workflowInputs": {
          "mappingMode": "defineBelow",
          "value": {
            "tool_name": "={{ $json.body.tool_name }}",
            "clickup_task_id": "={{ $json.body.clickup_task_id }}",
            "tool_input_json": "={{ $json.body.tool_input_json }}"
          },
          "matchingColumns": [],
          "attemptToConvertTypes": false,
          "convertFieldsToString": false
        },
        "options": {}
      },
      "onError": "continueErrorOutput"
    },
    {
      "id": "build-bridge-response",
      "name": "Build Bridge Response",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.code",
      "typeVersion": 2,
      "position": [
        920,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "Normalize the handler output into {tool_result_content_json, new_warnings_json}. If the handler threw (no content), build a fail-soft text result + a WARN - the waiter ALWAYS posts a tool result, so a handler failure degrades the run, never deadlocks the session. runOnceForEachItem so the 4 incoming (extract/tail x success/error) connections do NOT trigger per-connection re-runs (only the one fired branch delivers an item).",
      "parameters": {
        "mode": "runOnceForEachItem",
        "jsCode": "const h = $json || {};\nlet content = h.tool_result_content_json;\nlet warns = h.new_warnings_json;\nif (!content) {\n  content = JSON.stringify([{ type: 'text', text: 'Pobranie kontekstu zadania nie powiodlo sie (blad narzedzia). Pracuj na podstawie dostepnego kontekstu i nie zglaszaj tego jako bledu.' }]);\n  warns = JSON.stringify([{ source: 'session-waiter/tool-bridge-failed', err: String((h.error && (h.error.message || h.error)) || 'brak wyniku narzedzia').slice(0, 300), severity: 'WARN' }]);\n}\nreturn { json: { tool_result_content_json: content, new_warnings_json: warns || '[]', status: h.status || 'ok' } };"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "respond-bridge",
      "name": "Respond",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.respondToWebhook",
      "typeVersion": 1.1,
      "position": [
        1140,
        300
      ],
      "notes": "Return the normalized tool result to the waiter, which posts it as user.custom_tool_result and resumes the session.",
      "parameters": {
        "respondWith": "firstIncomingItem",
        "options": {
          "responseCode": 200
        }
      }
    }
  ],
